<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss short-time work down in March.</title>
<headline>Swiss short-time work down in March.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people on short-time work in Switzerland fell to 13,227 in March, down 3,025 or 18.6 percent from February, the Swiss Federal Office of Trade, Industry and Labour said.</p>
<p>The number of companies affected dropped by 167 or 10.4 percent to 1,445.</p>
<p>Lost working hours fell by 210,478 or 20.7 percent to 806,028.</p>
<p>In March 1996, 1.2 million hours had been lost among 20,028 workers at 1,909 companies.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
